IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mac-dates`

-- Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 (NSW) -- the legacy compulsory third-party (CTP) scheme, from the seat of the
-- person injured in a motor accident (or the relative claiming for a death). The Act governs motor accidents from its
-- commencement in 1999 until the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 took over (s 3AA).
--
-- SEAT: the injured person, the claimant. Every exported question is one that person would ask: "Does the scheme cover
-- me?", "Can I claim if no one was at fault?", "Can my child claim?", "Can I claim against the Nominal Defendant?", "Can I
-- get my early treatment costs paid?", "By when must I report, notify and claim?", "Can my late claim still go ahead?",
-- "Has the insurer answered on liability?", "By when must it make me an offer?", "By when must I go to court?", "Is my
-- claim taken to be withdrawn?". The insurer, the Nominal Defendant, the Authority, the Commission and the court get no
-- seat: what they do is encoded as what it means for the claimant.
--
-- Provisions: ss 3, 3AA, 3A, 3B (application); Part 1.2, ss 7A-7P (blameless accidents and children); ss 33, 34, 34A,
-- 35A (Nominal Defendant); Part 3.2, ss 46-51 (early payment); ss 70, 72, 73, 76 (reporting, time for claims, late and
-- defective claims); ss 81, 82 (insurer's notice on liability, offer of settlement); ss 85, 85B, 86 (the claimant's
-- duties and their consequences); ss 108, 109, 110 (court proceedings). Damages (Chapter 5) are in mac-damages.l4.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "only if", "unless", "where", a flat "does not apply", "cannot", "is not entitled"), or
-- NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 16 June 2022; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 -- claims`

§§ `The nouns`

-- Who was at fault ("fault means negligence or any other tort", s 3).
DECLARE `Who was at fault` IS ONE OF
    `the owner or driver of a vehicle involved`
    `no one: a blameless accident`
    `only someone who is not an owner or driver of a vehicle involved, or only me`

-- The vehicle that caused the injury, for a claim against the Nominal Defendant (ss 33, 34).
DECLARE `The vehicle that caused my injury` IS ONE OF
    `it was not an insured motor vehicle`
    `its identity cannot be established`
    `it was an insured motor vehicle`

-- The kinds of expense a child's special entitlement may cover (s 7J(3)), and anything else.
DECLARE `The expense I am asking about` IS ONE OF
    `hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses`
    `rehabilitation expenses`
    `respite care expenses`
    `attendant care services expenses`
    `funeral or cremation expenses`
    `another kind of loss`

-- How the child's case stands under Part 1.2 (ss 7F, 7K, 7L, 7P).
DECLARE `How my child's case stands` IS ONE OF
    `no owner or driver was at fault, and the accident was not blameless (Division 2)`
    `the accident was blameless (Division 1)`
    `the owner or driver of a vehicle was at fault`

-- The ground on which an insurer may reject a claim before assessment (ss 34A, 70, 73, 76).
DECLARE `The ground the insurer may reject my claim on` IS ONE OF
    `the claim was made late (s 73)`
    `the accident was not reported to police within 28 days (s 70)`
    `the notice of claim did not comply with s 74`
    `no due inquiry and search was made to identify the vehicle (s 34A)`

-- What the insurer did within the first two months.
DECLARE `What the insurer did about that ground` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `it rejected the claim on that ground`
    `it asked me for an explanation or to make due inquiry and search`

-- The answers about provisional liability (s 50).
DECLARE `Where provisional liability stands` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer has accepted provisional liability`
    `the insurer is taken to have accepted provisional liability`
    `the insurer has not accepted provisional liability`
    `the insurer still has time to give notice`

-- What the insurer's written notice under s 81 said.
DECLARE `What the insurer's notice said` IS ONE OF
    `it admits liability`
    `it admits liability in part`
    `it denies liability`

-- The answers about liability (s 81).
DECLARE `Where liability stands` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer admits liability`
    `the insurer admits liability in part`
    `the insurer denies liability`
    `the insurer is taken to have wholly denied liability`
    `the insurer still has time to answer`

-- The parties and acts of the regulative rules.
DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF `the insurer`, `the claimant`
DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF
    `submit the accident notification form`
    `give written notice on provisional liability`
    `reject the claim on the ground or ask for an explanation`
    `reject the explanation`
    `give written notice admitting or denying liability`
    `commence court proceedings`
    `provide the relevant particulars`

§§ `Running a rule against what happened`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not before day 0` n MEANS IF n LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE n

-- A rule is kept when its trace, with the act done on the day given (counted from the rule's start), is FULFILLED. Where
-- the act was not done, the trace waits until the day asked about, and is not FULFILLED.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
      `the party` IS A `Claim party`
      `the act` IS A `Claim act`
      `it was done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A NUMBER
      `the day asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the rule was kept` `the rule` `the party` `the act` `it was done` `the day it was done` `the day asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `it was done`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the party` `the act` (`not before day 0` `the day it was done`))
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL (`not before day 0` `the day asked about`))

§§ `ss 3, 3AA, 3A, 3B, 67, 122 -- does the scheme cover my injury`

-- s 3AA(1) "this Act does not apply to or in respect of a motor accident occurring after the commencement of the Motor
-- Accident Injuries Act 2017" (a flat negative). s 67(1) Chapter 4 applies to a claim for an accident "occurring after
-- the commencement of this Act"; s 122(2) Chapter 5 "does not apply to ... a motor accident occurring before" it (the
-- Motor Accidents Act 1988 governs those; fork F2). s 3A(1) the Act "applies only in respect of the death of or injury to
-- a person that is caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a motor vehicle in the use or operation of the vehicle
-- and only if" it is caused during (a) the driving of the vehicle, (b) a collision or action to avoid one, (c) the vehicle
-- running out of control, or (d) a dangerous situation caused by one of these. s 3A(2) the Act "does not apply in respect
-- of an injury that arises gradually from a series of incidents". s 3B(1) Chapters 3-6 are "limited to" death or injury
-- caused by a motor accident for which the vehicle has motor accident insurance cover (s 3B(2): a NSW third-party
-- policy, another place's or the Commonwealth's CTP cover, a Commonwealth vehicle, or a right of action against the
-- Nominal Defendant), or that gives rise to a work injury claim (other than a coal miner's). Where no owner or driver was
-- at fault, Part 1.2 may deem fault: that is asked by the next two questions, so this one answers NOTHING (fork F3).
@export Does the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 (the CTP scheme before the 2017 Act) cover my death or injury claim from this motor accident (ss 3, 3AA, 3A, 3B, 67, 122)?
GIVEN `the accident happened after the 1999 Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened after the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 commenced (October 1999); earlier accidents fall under the Motor Accidents Act 1988
      `the accident happened after the 2017 Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened after the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 commenced (1 December 2017); later accidents fall under that Act instead
      `who was at fault` IS A `Who was at fault` @desc Who was at fault (negligent, or otherwise committed a tort) in causing the injury. One of: "the owner or driver of a vehicle involved", "no one: a blameless accident", "only someone who is not an owner or driver of a vehicle involved, or only me"
      `it happened during driving, a collision, loss of control or a resulting dangerous situation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death or injury was caused during the driving of the vehicle, a collision (or action taken to avoid one) with it, the vehicle running out of control, or a dangerous situation caused by one of those
      `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents rather than from one accident
      `the vehicle had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle had motor accident insurance cover for the accident: a NSW green slip (third-party policy), compulsory third-party cover under another State's or the Commonwealth's law, ownership by the Commonwealth, or a right of action against the Nominal Defendant (an uninsured or unidentified vehicle)
      `it gives rise to a work injury claim against my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a worker injured (or killed) through your employer's negligence or other tort, so that it is a work injury claim under Part 5 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 (not counting a coal miner's claim)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the 1999 scheme cover my claim` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the accident happened after the 2017 Act commenced` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3AA(1)
           IF (NOT `the accident happened after the 1999 Act commenced`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- ss 67(1), 122(2) (fork F2)
           IF `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3A(2)
           IF (NOT `it happened during driving, a collision, loss of control or a resulting dangerous situation`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3A(1) "only if"
           IF (NOT (`the vehicle had motor accident insurance cover` OR `it gives rise to a work injury claim against my employer`)) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3B(1) "limited to"
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `who was at fault`
               WHEN `the owner or driver of a vehicle involved` THEN JUST TRUE
               OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (Part 1.2 may deem fault; asked by the blameless-accident and child questions; fork F3)

§§ `Part 1.2 Division 1 -- blameless accidents (ss 7A-7E, 7I)`

-- s 7A "blameless motor accident means a motor accident not caused by the fault of the owner or driver of any motor
-- vehicle involved in the accident in the use or operation of the vehicle and not caused by the fault of any other
-- person." s 7B(1) the death or injury that results from a blameless motor accident "involving a motor vehicle that has
-- motor accident insurance cover for the accident" is deemed to have been caused by the fault of the owner or driver.
-- s 7C: the claimant's averment that the accident was blameless is evidence of it unless contradicted. s 7D "This
-- Division applies only in respect of motor accidents that occur in the State after the commencement of this Division"
-- (the Division was inserted by the Motor Accidents Compensation Amendment Act 2006; its commencement date is not in the
-- deposited text and is asked). s 7E(1) "There is no entitlement to recover damages under this Division in respect of the
-- death of or injury to the driver of a motor vehicle if the motor accident concerned was caused by an act or omission of
-- that driver", even an involuntary one, one that is not fault, or one that is not the sole cause (s 7E(2)). s 7F:
-- contributory negligence may still reduce damages. s 7I: other entitlements are not affected.
@export If no one was at fault in my motor accident, can I still claim damages as if the owner or driver had been at fault, under the blameless accident rules (ss 7A-7E)?
GIVEN `the accident happened after the 2017 Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened after the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 commenced (1 December 2017)
      `the accident happened in NSW after Part 1.2 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in New South Wales after Part 1.2 of the Act (no-fault claims, inserted by the Motor Accidents Compensation Amendment Act 2006) commenced
      `it happened during driving, a collision, loss of control or a resulting dangerous situation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death or injury was caused during the driving of a vehicle, a collision (or action taken to avoid one) with it, the vehicle running out of control, or a dangerous situation caused by one of those
      `no owner or driver and no other person was at fault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident was caused by no one's fault: not by the owner or driver of any vehicle involved, and not by any other person (a blameless accident)
      `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a vehicle involved in the accident had motor accident insurance cover for it (a NSW green slip, another place's or the Commonwealth's compulsory cover, a Commonwealth vehicle, or a Nominal Defendant claim)
      `I was a driver whose act or omission caused the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver of a vehicle and the accident was caused by something you did or failed to do, even involuntarily (for example a sudden illness), even if it was not your fault and not the only cause
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I claim for a blameless accident` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the accident happened after the 2017 Act commenced` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3AA(1)
           IF (NOT `the accident happened in NSW after Part 1.2 commenced`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7D "applies only"
           IF (NOT `it happened during driving, a collision, loss of control or a resulting dangerous situation`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3 "motor accident means"
           IF (NOT `no owner or driver and no other person was at fault`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7A "means" (a fault claim may lie instead, s 7I)
           IF (NOT `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7B(1), the deeming is limited to a vehicle with cover
           IF `I was a driver whose act or omission caused the accident` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7E(1)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 1.2 Division 2 -- children (ss 7J, 7K, 7L, 7P)`

-- s 7J(1) if the death of or injury to a child "results from a motor accident not caused by the fault of the owner or
-- driver of a motor vehicle", it is deemed caused by that fault, for the special entitlement, "if the motor vehicle was
-- involved in the accident and has motor accident insurance cover". s 7J(5) "The motor accident must occur in the State
-- after the commencement of this Division and the child must be a resident of the State at the time of the motor
-- accident." s 7J(6) "child means a person who is under 16 years of age at the time of the motor accident." s 7K(1) the
-- Division applies even if the child was at fault; s 7K(2) "A court is not to award damages pursuant to this Division
-- ... if the court is satisfied that" the child's conduct, on the balance of probabilities, was a serious offence (one
-- punishable by imprisonment for 6 months or more, s 7K(3)) and contributed materially (the court's judgment, asked).
-- s 7P(1) "This Division does not apply in a case to which Division 1 ... applies". Where the owner or driver was at
-- fault, the child claims in the ordinary way and s 7L protects the special-entitlement kind of damages.
@export Does my child have the special no-fault entitlement for children injured or killed in a motor accident where no owner or driver was at fault (ss 7J, 7K, 7P)?
GIVEN `the accident happened after the 2017 Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened after the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 commenced (1 December 2017)
      `the accident happened in NSW after Part 1.2 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in New South Wales after Part 1.2 of the Act (no-fault claims, inserted by the Motor Accidents Compensation Amendment Act 2006) commenced
      `my child was under 16 at the time of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was under 16 years of age at the time of the accident
      `my child was resident in NSW at the time of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was a resident of New South Wales at the time of the accident
      `it happened during driving, a collision, loss of control or a resulting dangerous situation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death or injury was caused during the driving of a vehicle, a collision (or action taken to avoid one) with it, the vehicle running out of control, or a dangerous situation caused by one of those
      `how my child's case stands` IS A `How my child's case stands` @desc Who was at fault. One of: "no owner or driver was at fault, and the accident was not blameless (Division 2)" (for example your child, or someone who was not driving, was at fault), "the accident was blameless (Division 1)" (no one at all was at fault), "the owner or driver of a vehicle was at fault"
      `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a vehicle involved in the accident had motor accident insurance cover for it (a NSW green slip, another place's or the Commonwealth's compulsory cover, a Commonwealth vehicle, or a Nominal Defendant claim)
      `the court is satisfied my child's serious offence contributed materially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that the injury or death happened at the time of, or after, conduct of your child that on the balance of probabilities was an offence punishable by 6 months' imprisonment or more, and that this conduct contributed materially to the injury or death or its risk
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my child have the special entitlement` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the accident happened after the 2017 Act commenced` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3AA(1)
           IF (NOT `the accident happened in NSW after Part 1.2 commenced`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7J(5) "must occur"
           IF (NOT `my child was under 16 at the time of the accident`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7J(6) "child means"
           IF (NOT `my child was resident in NSW at the time of the accident`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7J(5)
           IF (NOT `it happened during driving, a collision, loss of control or a resulting dangerous situation`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3 "motor accident means"
           IF (NOT (`how my child's case stands` EQUALS `no owner or driver was at fault, and the accident was not blameless (Division 2)`)) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7J(1) "if ... not caused by the fault"; s 7P(1) flat
           IF (NOT `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7J(1) "if the motor vehicle ... has motor accident insurance cover"
           IF `the court is satisfied my child's serious offence contributed materially` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7K(2) "is not to award"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 7J(3) "The special entitlement to recover damages conferred by this Division is an entitlement to recover damages for
-- the following ... (a) hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses, (b) rehabilitation expenses, (c) respite care
-- expenses, (d) attendant care services expenses, (e) funeral or cremation expenses." Read as a closed definition (fork
-- F4): another kind of loss is outside the special entitlement (JUST FALSE). s 7J(4): funeral or cremation expenses are
-- recovered under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897, and nothing else under that Act.
@export Does the children's special no-fault entitlement cover this kind of expense or loss (s 7J(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the expense` IS A `The expense I am asking about` @desc The expense or loss you are asking about. One of: "hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses", "rehabilitation expenses", "respite care expenses", "attendant care services expenses", "funeral or cremation expenses" (recovered under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897), "another kind of loss" (for example pain and suffering, or loss of earnings)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the special entitlement cover this expense` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the expense`
    WHEN `another kind of loss` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7J(3) "is an entitlement to recover damages for the following" (fork F4)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 7F (Division 1) "This Division does not prevent the reduction of damages by reason of the contributory negligence of
-- the deceased or injured person." s 7K(5) (Division 2) "There is to be no reduction of the damages provided for by this
-- Division by reason of the contributory negligence of the deceased or injured person, except as provided by this
-- section." s 7L: where the child would have the special entitlement but for the owner's or driver's fault, damages of
-- the special-entitlement kind are "not to be reduced on account of the contributory negligence of the child". s 7P(2):
-- the same where the child would have it but for Division 1 applying. Otherwise the ordinary law of contributory
-- negligence (s 138) applies, so a reduction can be made (JUST TRUE: "can", if the court finds contributory negligence).
@export Can my child's damages of this kind be reduced because of my child's own contributory negligence (ss 7F, 7K(5), 7L, 7P(2))?
GIVEN `how my child's case stands` IS A `How my child's case stands` @desc Who was at fault. One of: "no owner or driver was at fault, and the accident was not blameless (Division 2)", "the accident was blameless (Division 1)", "the owner or driver of a vehicle was at fault"
      `the expense` IS A `The expense I am asking about` @desc The kind of damages. One of: "hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses", "rehabilitation expenses", "respite care expenses", "attendant care services expenses", "funeral or cremation expenses", "another kind of loss"
      `my child otherwise meets the special entitlement's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, leaving aside who was at fault, your child meets the special entitlement's other conditions: under 16 and resident in NSW at the time, the accident in NSW after Part 1.2 commenced, and a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my child's damages be reduced for contributory negligence` MEANS
    IF `the expense` EQUALS `another kind of loss`
    THEN CONSIDER `how my child's case stands`
         WHEN `no owner or driver was at fault, and the accident was not blameless (Division 2)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (Division 2 gives no such damages; the text is silent)
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- ss 7F, 138(1)
    ELSE CONSIDER `how my child's case stands`
         WHEN `no owner or driver was at fault, and the accident was not blameless (Division 2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7K(5)
         OTHERWISE
             IF `my child otherwise meets the special entitlement's conditions`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- ss 7L, 7P(2)
             ELSE JUST TRUE  -- ss 7F, 138(1)

§§ `ss 33, 34, 34A, 35A -- the Nominal Defendant`

-- s 33(1) an action for damages caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a motor vehicle "that is not an insured
-- motor vehicle in the use or operation of the vehicle on a road in New South Wales may be brought against the Nominal
-- Defendant"; s 34(1) likewise "if the identity of the vehicle cannot be established". s 34(1AA) "A claim cannot be made
-- against the Nominal Defendant under this section unless due inquiry and search has been made to establish the identity
-- of the motor vehicle concerned." ss 33(3A), 34(1A): no right of action for a trespasser on a road related area that is
-- open to the public. s 33(4): none (a) for a Commonwealth vehicle, (c) for a vehicle registered elsewhere with that
-- place's compulsory cover, (b) where s 35 (trailers) applies, (d) where the regulations say so (not deposited; fork
-- F5). s 35A: none for damages attributable to an act of terrorism (on or after 1 January 2002 and before a day to be
-- proclaimed; s 15A(2) decides what is terrorism, asked). An insured vehicle: claim against its insurer (JUST FALSE here).
@export Can I bring my claim against the Nominal Defendant because the vehicle was uninsured or cannot be identified (ss 33, 34, 35A)?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `The vehicle that caused my injury` @desc The vehicle whose owner or driver was at fault. One of: "it was not an insured motor vehicle" (no green slip), "its identity cannot be established" (for example a hit-and-run), "it was an insured motor vehicle"
      `it was caused by the owner's or driver's fault on a road in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death or injury was caused by the fault of the vehicle's owner or driver in using or operating it on a road in New South Wales
      `I was a trespasser on a road related area open to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened on a road related area that counts as such because it is open to or used by the public for driving, riding or parking (for example a car park), and you were a trespasser there
      `the vehicle was owned by the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was owned by the Commonwealth or by a person or body representing the Commonwealth
      `the vehicle was registered elsewhere and covered by that place's compulsory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was registered under the law of another State or Territory (or of the Commonwealth) and covered by its compulsory third-party insurance or accident compensation scheme
      `the damages are attributable to an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the damages are attributable to an act that can reasonably be characterised as an act of terrorism (as section 15A(2) defines it), done on or after 1 January 2002
      `due inquiry and search was made to identify the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether due inquiry and search was made to establish the identity of the vehicle (this matters only for an unidentified vehicle)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I claim against the Nominal Defendant` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the vehicle` EQUALS `it was an insured motor vehicle` THEN JUST FALSE  -- ss 33(1), 34(1): claim against the vehicle's insurer
           IF (NOT `it was caused by the owner's or driver's fault on a road in NSW`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- ss 33(1), 34(1)
           IF `I was a trespasser on a road related area open to the public` THEN JUST FALSE  -- ss 33(3A), 34(1A)
           IF `the damages are attributable to an act of terrorism` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 35A(1)
           IF `the vehicle` EQUALS `its identity cannot be established` THEN `the unidentified vehicle answer`
           IF `the vehicle was owned by the Commonwealth` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 33(4)(a)
           IF `the vehicle was registered elsewhere and covered by that place's compulsory scheme` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 33(4)(c)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- s 33(1) (fork F5: s 33(4)(b), (d) not asked)
    WHERE
        `the unidentified vehicle answer` MEANS
            IF `due inquiry and search was made to identify the vehicle`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 34(1AA) "cannot be made ... unless"

§§ `Part 3.2 -- early payment of treatment expenses and lost earnings (ss 46-51)`

-- s 48 "An injured person is not entitled to payment for treatment expenses or lost earnings under this Part unless--
-- (a) a police officer attended the motor accident ... or the motor accident has been officially reported to a police
-- officer by or on behalf of the injured person, and (b) an accident notification form has been completed by or on behalf
-- of the injured person and submitted to the insurer, and (c) the accident notification form is submitted to the insurer
-- within 28 days after the motor accident (or within such other period as the form requires), and (d) the accident
-- notification form contains a declaration ... that the person's injuries are a direct result of the motor accident."
-- The form's own period is not deposited: 28 days is used (fork F6). Written as a rule: the injured person must submit
-- the form within 28 days. s 46A: Part 3.2 applies "despite section 3A (1)": fault is not needed.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 48(b), (c) -- the injured person must submit the accident notification form within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `submit the accident notification form`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "accident notification form not submitted to the insurer within 28 days after the motor accident (s 48(c)); no early payment under Part 3.2"

@export By when must I submit the accident notification form to the insurer to get early payment of my treatment expenses and lost earnings (s 48(c))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I submit the accident notification form` MEANS `the day of the accident` `plus days` 28

-- s 47A(1) payment is not required if the injury occurred at the time of, or following, the injured person's conduct
-- that on the balance of probabilities is a serious offence (punishable by 6 months' imprisonment or more), and the
-- conduct contributed materially. Who weighs this is not said; it is asked as a fact. s 50(7) the insurer must pay "only
-- if the insurer has accepted or is taken to have accepted provisional liability" (asked here; see the next question).
-- s 47(3) payment is not required for expenses or earnings after a claim is made (see the amount question).
@export Am I entitled to early payment of my treatment expenses and lost earnings by the CTP insurer, whoever was at fault (ss 46A, 47A, 48, 50(7))?
GIVEN `a police officer attended or the accident was officially reported to police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a police officer attended the accident, or the accident was officially reported to a police officer by you or on your behalf
      `I submitted an accident notification form to the insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an accident notification form was completed by you or for you and submitted to the CTP insurer
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the day I submitted the form` IS A DATE @desc The day the accident notification form was submitted to the insurer (any day if it was not)
      `the form declares my injuries are a direct result of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the form contains a declaration, by you or for you, that your injuries are a direct result of the motor accident
      `my serious offence contributed materially to my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury happened at the time of, or after, your own conduct that on the balance of probabilities was an offence punishable by 6 months' imprisonment or more, and that conduct contributed materially to the injury or its risk
      `the insurer has accepted or is taken to have accepted provisional liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has accepted provisional liability for your treatment expenses and lost earnings, or is taken to have accepted it (see the question on provisional liability)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to early payment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `a police officer attended or the accident was officially reported to police`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 48(a)
           IF (NOT `the form was submitted in time`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 48(b), (c)
           IF (NOT `the form declares my injuries are a direct result of the accident`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 48(d)
           IF `my serious offence contributed materially to my injury` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 47A(1)
           IF (NOT `the insurer has accepted or is taken to have accepted provisional liability`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 50(7) "only if"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the form was submitted in time` MEANS
            `the rule was kept` (`s 48(b), (c) -- the injured person must submit the accident notification form within 28 days`) `the claimant` `submit the accident notification form` `I submitted an accident notification form to the insurer` (`the days from` `the day of the accident` `to` `the day I submitted the form`) 29

-- s 50(1), (3) the insurer "must give written notice to an injured person who has duly submitted a completed accident
-- notification form ... stating whether or not the insurer accepts provisional liability", "within 10 days after the
-- insurer receives the accident notification form" (the regulations may change the period: not deposited, fork F6).
-- s 50(4) "If the insurer fails to notify the injured person in accordance with this section, the insurer is taken to
-- have accepted provisional liability." s 50(5): not so for the Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle (s 34),
-- which accepts only by written notice. s 50(6): an insurer may accept after denying. A late notice refusing it does not
-- undo the acceptance taken under s 50(4) (fork F7).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 50(1), (3) -- the insurer must give notice on provisional liability within 10 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `give written notice on provisional liability`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "no written notice on provisional liability within 10 days after receiving the accident notification form (s 50(3)); the insurer is taken to have accepted provisional liability (s 50(4))"

@export Has the CTP insurer accepted provisional liability for my treatment expenses and lost earnings, or is it taken to have accepted it (s 50)?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received my form` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received your completed accident notification form
      `the insurer has given me written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you written notice saying whether it accepts provisional liability
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer gave you that notice (any day if it has not)
      `the notice accepts provisional liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice (or the latest notice) accepts provisional liability
      `the insurer acts for the Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is, or is acting for, the Nominal Defendant because the vehicle could not be identified (s 34)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A `Where provisional liability stands`
`Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the insurer has given me written notice` AND `the notice accepts provisional liability` THEN `the insurer has accepted provisional liability`  -- s 50(1), (6)
           IF `notice in time` THEN `the insurer has not accepted provisional liability`
           IF `the insurer has given me written notice` OR `the time is up` THEN `the late answer`
           OTHERWISE `the insurer still has time to give notice`
    WHERE
        `notice in time` MEANS
            `the rule was kept` (`s 50(1), (3) -- the insurer must give notice on provisional liability within 10 days`) `the insurer` `give written notice on provisional liability` `the insurer has given me written notice` (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my form` `to` `the day of the notice`) (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my form` `to` `today`)
        `the time is up` MEANS `the days from` `the day the insurer received my form` `to` `today` GREATER THAN 10
        `the late answer` MEANS
            IF `the insurer acts for the Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle`
            THEN `the insurer has not accepted provisional liability`  -- s 50(5)
            ELSE `the insurer is taken to have accepted provisional liability`  -- s 50(4) (fork F7)

-- s 51(1) "The maximum amount that an insurer is required to pay under this Part as the total amount of treatment
-- expenses and lost earnings of an injured person is $5,000 or such other amount as may be determined by the Authority"
-- (by Gazette order, s 51(2); not deposited: the amount is asked). s 51(4) only for treatment provided or earnings lost
-- "within 6 months after the motor accident". s 51(5) "Treatment expenses are to be paid in priority to lost earnings
-- and ... payment for lost earnings ... is to be made only to the extent that payment for treatment expenses for
-- treatment provided in that 6 months will not exceed the maximum". s 47(2), (3): nothing already paid on a claim or
-- under Part 3.3, and nothing incurred after a claim is made. s 53: only reasonable and necessary treatment related to
-- the injury. The amounts asked are those that meet ss 47, 52 and 53.
@export At most how much early payment must the CTP insurer make for my treatment expenses and lost earnings in the first 6 months (ss 47, 51)?
GIVEN `my treatment expenses in the 6 months` IS A NUMBER @desc Your reasonable and necessary treatment expenses (hospital, medical, pharmaceutical, rehabilitation; not attendant care), in dollars, for treatment within 6 months after the accident and before you made a claim, not already paid on a claim or under Part 3.3
      `my lost earnings in the 6 months` IS A NUMBER @desc Your past loss of earnings, in dollars, suffered within 6 months after the accident and before you made a claim
      `the maximum in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum total amount in dollars: $5,000 under section 51(1), unless the Authority has varied it by order published in the Gazette
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much early payment must the insurer make` MEANS
    `the treatment paid` PLUS `the earnings paid`
    WHERE
        `the treatment paid` MEANS `the smaller of` `my treatment expenses in the 6 months` `and` `the maximum in force`
        `the earnings paid`  MEANS `the smaller of` `my lost earnings in the 6 months` `and` (`the maximum in force` MINUS `the treatment paid`)

§§ `ss 70, 72 -- reporting the accident and making the claim`

-- s 70(1) "Unless a police officer attended the motor accident, a motor accident that gives rise to a claim must be
-- reported to a police officer by or on behalf of the claimant within 28 days after the motor accident."
@export If no police officer attended my accident, by when must I report it to police (s 70(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `a police officer attended the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a police officer attended the accident
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I report the accident to police` MEANS
    IF `a police officer attended the accident`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no duty: "Unless a police officer attended")
    ELSE JUST (`the day of the accident` `plus days` 28)

-- s 72(1) "A claim must be made within 6 months after the relevant date for the claim. The relevant date is the date of
-- the motor accident ... unless the claim is made in respect of the death of a person, in which case the relevant date is
-- the date of the person's death." s 72(2): notice to the person's third-party insurer (or the person). After that day
-- the claim is a late claim, allowed only with a full and satisfactory explanation (s 73).
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, `the claim is for a death` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the relevant date` `the day of the accident` `the claim is for a death` `the day of death` MEANS
    IF `the claim is for a death` THEN `the day of death` ELSE `the day of the accident`

@export By when must I make my claim (give notice of it to the CTP insurer) without needing to explain the delay (ss 72(1), 73(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the claim is for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for the death of a person (for example by a relative)
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died (any day if the claim is not for a death)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I make my claim` MEANS
    (`the relevant date` `the day of the accident` `the claim is for a death` `the day of death`) `plus months` 6

§§ `ss 34A, 70, 73, 76 -- late or defective claims, and the insurer's two months`

-- Four grounds share one shape. The insurer "loses the right to reject" the claim on the ground if it "(a) does not,
-- within 2 months after receiving the claim, reject the claim on [that ground] or ask the claimant to provide a full and
-- satisfactory explanation", or "(b) does not, within 2 months after receiving an explanation ..., reject the
-- explanation" (ss 70(4), 73(4); s 34A(2) the same for due inquiry and search, the explanation being notice of efforts
-- to identify the vehicle). For s 74 (s 76(2)) only a rejection within 2 months keeps the right: there is no request
-- and no second step. Written as two rules: the insurer must act within the two months, lest it lose the right.
GIVEN `the days in the two months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`ss 34A(2)(a), 70(4)(a), 73(4)(a), 76(2) -- the insurer must reject or ask within 2 months after receiving the claim` `the days in the two months` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `reject the claim on the ground or ask for an explanation`
    WITHIN `the days in the two months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "the claim was neither rejected on the ground nor an explanation asked for within 2 months after the insurer received it; the insurer loses the right to reject it on that ground"

GIVEN `the days in the two months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`ss 34A(2)(b), 70(4)(b), 73(4)(b) -- the insurer must reject the explanation within 2 months after receiving it` `the days in the two months` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `reject the explanation`
    WITHIN `the days in the two months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "the explanation was not rejected within 2 months after the insurer received it; the insurer loses the right to reject the claim on that ground"

@export Has the insurer (or the Nominal Defendant) lost the right to reject my claim on this ground because it did not act within 2 months (ss 34A(2), 70(4), 73(4), 76(2))?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `The ground the insurer may reject my claim on` @desc The ground. One of: "the claim was made late (s 73)", "the accident was not reported to police within 28 days (s 70)", "the notice of claim did not comply with s 74", "no due inquiry and search was made to identify the vehicle (s 34A)"
      `the day the insurer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer (or the person you claimed against, or the Nominal Defendant) received your claim
      `what the insurer did` IS A `What the insurer did about that ground` @desc What the insurer did about that ground after receiving the claim. One of: "nothing", "it rejected the claim on that ground", "it asked me for an explanation or to make due inquiry and search"
      `the day the insurer did it` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer rejected the claim or made the request (any day if it did nothing)
      `I gave the insurer an explanation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has received your explanation for the delay or non-compliance (or, for an unidentified vehicle, notice of your efforts to identify it)
      `the day the insurer received my explanation` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received that explanation or notice (any day if none)
      `the insurer rejected my explanation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has rejected your explanation (or refused to accept that due inquiry and search was made)
      `the day the insurer rejected it` IS A DATE @desc The day it did so (any day if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` MEANS
    `first step lost` OR `second step lost`
    WHERE
        `the act counts` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what the insurer did`
            WHEN `nothing` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `it rejected the claim on that ground` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE (NOT (`the ground` EQUALS `the notice of claim did not comply with s 74`))
        `first window` MEANS `the days in the` 2 `months after` `the day the insurer received my claim`
        `first kept` MEANS
            `the rule was kept` (`ss 34A(2)(a), 70(4)(a), 73(4)(a), 76(2) -- the insurer must reject or ask within 2 months after receiving the claim` `first window`) `the insurer` `reject the claim on the ground or ask for an explanation` `the act counts` (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my claim` `to` `the day the insurer did it`) (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my claim` `to` `today`)
        `first step lost` MEANS
                (NOT `first kept`)
            AND (`the act counts` OR (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my claim` `to` `today` GREATER THAN `first window`))
        `second window` MEANS `the days in the` 2 `months after` `the day the insurer received my explanation`
        `second kept` MEANS
            `the rule was kept` (`ss 34A(2)(b), 70(4)(b), 73(4)(b) -- the insurer must reject the explanation within 2 months after receiving it` `second window`) `the insurer` `reject the explanation` `the insurer rejected my explanation` (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my explanation` `to` `the day the insurer rejected it`) (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my explanation` `to` `today`)
        `second step lost` MEANS
                (NOT (`the ground` EQUALS `the notice of claim did not comply with s 74`))
            AND `I gave the insurer an explanation`
            AND (NOT `second kept`)
            AND (`the insurer rejected my explanation` OR (`the days from` `the day the insurer received my explanation` `to` `today` GREATER THAN `second window`))

-- ss 34A(1), 70(3), 73(3), 76(1): where the ground exists, "the claim cannot be referred for assessment under Part 4.4
-- unless-- (a) the insurer has lost the right to reject the claim on [that ground], or (b) the Commission has, on the
-- assessment of a dispute ..., assessed [in the claimant's favour], or (c) the claim is referred only for a certificate
-- of exemption from assessment". Whether the Commission so assessed is asked.
@export My claim is late or has another defect the insurer may reject it for: can it still be referred to the Personal Injury Commission for assessment (ss 34A(1), 70(3), 73(3), 76(1))?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `The ground the insurer may reject my claim on` @desc The defect in your claim. One of: "the claim was made late (s 73)", "the accident was not reported to police within 28 days (s 70)", "the notice of claim did not comply with s 74", "no due inquiry and search was made to identify the vehicle (s 34A)"
      `the day the insurer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer (or the person you claimed against, or the Nominal Defendant) received your claim
      `what the insurer did` IS A `What the insurer did about that ground` @desc What the insurer did about that ground after receiving the claim. One of: "nothing", "it rejected the claim on that ground", "it asked me for an explanation or to make due inquiry and search"
      `the day the insurer did it` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer rejected the claim or made the request (any day if it did nothing)
      `I gave the insurer an explanation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has received your explanation (or, for an unidentified vehicle, notice of your efforts to identify it)
      `the day the insurer received my explanation` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received that explanation or notice (any day if none)
      `the insurer rejected my explanation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has rejected your explanation (or refused to accept that due inquiry and search was made)
      `the day the insurer rejected it` IS A DATE @desc The day it did so (any day if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `the Commission assessed the dispute in my favour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Personal Injury Commission, assessing the dispute, found in your favour (a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay; sufficient cause for the late police report and a report within a reasonable period; the non-compliance with s 74 technical and of no significance; or due inquiry and search made)
      `I am referring it only for a certificate of exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are referring the claim only for a certificate of exemption from assessment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my claim still be referred for assessment` MEANS
    IF     `the right is lost`
        OR `the Commission assessed the dispute in my favour`
        OR `I am referring it only for a certificate of exemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- "cannot be referred ... unless"
    WHERE
        `the right is lost` MEANS `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `the ground` `the day the insurer received my claim` `what the insurer did` `the day the insurer did it` `I gave the insurer an explanation` `the day the insurer received my explanation` `the insurer rejected my explanation` `the day the insurer rejected it` `today`

§§ `ss 81, 82 -- the insurer's answer on liability and its offer`

-- s 81(1) "It is the duty of an insurer to give written notice to the claimant as expeditiously as possible whether the
-- insurer admits or denies liability for the claim, but in any event within 3 months after the claimant gave notice of
-- the claim under section 72." s 81(3) "If the insurer fails to comply with this section, the insurer is taken to have
-- given notice to the claimant wholly denying liability for the claim." s 81(4): it may admit later.
GIVEN `the days in the three months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 81(1) -- the insurer must give written notice admitting or denying liability within 3 months` `the days in the three months` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `give written notice admitting or denying liability`
    WITHIN `the days in the three months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "no written notice admitting or denying liability within 3 months after notice of the claim (s 81(1)); the insurer is taken to have wholly denied liability (s 81(3))"

@export Has the CTP insurer admitted or denied liability for my claim, or is it taken to have wholly denied it (s 81)?
GIVEN `the day I gave notice of my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave notice of your claim under section 72
      `the insurer has given me written notice on liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you written notice saying whether it admits or denies liability
      `the day of that notice` IS A DATE @desc The day of that notice (any day if none)
      `what the notice said` IS A `What the insurer's notice said` @desc What the notice (or the latest notice) said. One of: "it admits liability", "it admits liability in part", "it denies liability" (any if none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A `Where liability stands`
`Where does liability stand` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `in time` OR `a late admission` THEN `what it said`
           IF `the insurer has given me written notice on liability` OR `the time is up` THEN `the insurer is taken to have wholly denied liability`  -- s 81(3)
           OTHERWISE `the insurer still has time to answer`
    WHERE
        `the window` MEANS `the days in the` 3 `months after` `the day I gave notice of my claim`
        `in time` MEANS
            `the rule was kept` (`s 81(1) -- the insurer must give written notice admitting or denying liability within 3 months` `the window`) `the insurer` `give written notice admitting or denying liability` `the insurer has given me written notice on liability` (`the days from` `the day I gave notice of my claim` `to` `the day of that notice`) (`the days from` `the day I gave notice of my claim` `to` `today`)
        `a late admission` MEANS `the insurer has given me written notice on liability` AND (NOT (`what the notice said` EQUALS `it denies liability`))  -- s 81(4)
        `the time is up` MEANS `the days from` `the day I gave notice of my claim` `to` `today` GREATER THAN `the window`
        `what it said` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what the notice said`
            WHEN `it admits liability` THEN `the insurer admits liability`
            WHEN `it admits liability in part` THEN `the insurer admits liability in part`  -- s 81(2)
            OTHERWISE `the insurer denies liability`

-- s 82(1) the insurer must make a reasonable offer of settlement (unless it wholly denies liability) "(a) within 1 month
-- after the injury is sufficiently recovered to enable the claim to be quantified, or (b) within 2 months after the
-- claimant has provided to the insurer all relevant particulars about the claim as required by section 85A, whichever is
-- the later." s 82(4) the section does not apply to (a) a claim for a death, (b) an injury not sufficiently recovered
-- within 3 years after the accident to quantify the claim, (c) a claim where a medical assessor declined to assess
-- permanent impairment because it has not become permanent. Where the section does not apply, or a day it counts from has
-- not yet come, the answer is NOTHING: there is no s 82 day.
@export By what day must the CTP insurer make me a reasonable offer of settlement (s 82)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the claim is for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for the death of a person
      `the insurer wholly denies liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer wholly denies liability for the claim
      `a medical assessor declined because my impairment is not yet permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical assessor has declined to assess your degree of permanent impairment because the impairment has not yet become permanent
      `my injury has recovered enough to quantify the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury has recovered sufficiently to enable the claim to be quantified
      `the day it recovered enough` IS A DATE @desc The day your injury became sufficiently recovered to quantify the claim (any day if not yet)
      `I have provided all relevant particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have provided the insurer with all relevant particulars of the claim (full details of your injuries, disabilities and impairments, and the economic and other losses claimed, s 85A)
      `the day I provided them` IS A DATE @desc The day you provided all of them (any day if not yet)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must the insurer make me an offer` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the claim is for a death` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 82(4)(a): the section does not apply)
           IF `the insurer wholly denies liability` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 82(1): no duty where liability is wholly denied)
           IF `a medical assessor declined because my impairment is not yet permanent` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 82(4)(c))
           IF (NOT `my injury has recovered enough to quantify the claim`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no day yet)
           IF `the day it recovered enough` `is after` (`the day of the accident` `plus years` 3) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 82(4)(b))
           IF (NOT `I have provided all relevant particulars`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no day yet)
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the later of` (`the day it recovered enough` `plus months` 1) `and` (`the day I provided them` `plus months` 2))

§§ `s 85B -- particulars not provided after 2 years and 6 months`

-- s 85B(1) if after 2 years and 6 months since the accident the claimant "has failed without reasonable excuse to provide
-- the insurer with all relevant particulars", the insurer "may by a written direction given to the claimant within 2
-- months after the end of that period require the claimant to provide those particulars". s 85B(3) "If the claimant does
-- not comply with the direction within 3 months after it is given, the claimant is taken to have withdrawn the claim."
-- s 85B(8): not where, at 2 years and 6 months, a medical assessor had declined to assess because the impairment was not
-- yet permanent. Reinstatement: s 85B(4), (6), (7) (next question).
GIVEN `the days in the three months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 85B(3) -- the claimant must provide the particulars within 3 months after the direction` `the days in the three months` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `provide the relevant particulars`
    WITHIN `the days in the three months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "the relevant particulars were not provided within 3 months after the insurer's direction; the claimant is taken to have withdrawn the claim (s 85B(3))"

@export Is my claim taken to have been withdrawn because I did not provide the relevant particulars the insurer directed me to provide (s 85B(1), (3), (8))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the insurer gave me a written direction to provide particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer gave you a written direction (in the approved form) to provide all relevant particulars of your claim
      `the day the direction was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the direction was given (any day if none)
      `at 2 years 6 months I had failed without reasonable excuse to provide them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, 2 years and 6 months after the accident, you had failed without reasonable excuse to provide all relevant particulars of the claim
      `at 2 years 6 months a medical assessor had declined to assess my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, 2 years and 6 months after the accident, a medical assessor had declined to assess your permanent impairment because it had not yet become permanent
      `I have provided the particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have provided the particulars the direction required
      `the day I provided the particulars` IS A DATE @desc The day you provided them (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my claim withdrawn for want of particulars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `at 2 years 6 months a medical assessor had declined to assess my impairment` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 85B(8)
           IF (NOT `the insurer gave me a written direction to provide particulars`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `at 2 years 6 months I had failed without reasonable excuse to provide them`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 85B(1) "If"
           IF (NOT `the direction was given in its window`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 85B(1) "within 2 months after the end of that period"
           IF `complied in time` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I have provided the particulars` OR `the time is up` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 85B(3)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- the 3 months have not yet run
    WHERE
        `the end of the period` MEANS `the day of the accident` `plus months` 30
        `the direction was given in its window` MEANS
                (`the day the direction was given` `is after` `the end of the period`)
            AND (NOT (`the day the direction was given` `is after` (`the end of the period` `plus months` 2)))
        `the window` MEANS `the days in the` 3 `months after` `the day the direction was given`
        `complied in time` MEANS
            `the rule was kept` (`s 85B(3) -- the claimant must provide the particulars within 3 months after the direction` `the window`) `the claimant` `provide the relevant particulars` `I have provided the particulars` (`the days from` `the day the direction was given` `to` `the day I provided the particulars`) (`the days from` `the day the direction was given` `to` `today`)
        `the time is up` MEANS `the days from` `the day the direction was given` `to` `today` GREATER THAN `the window`

-- s 85B(6) "If the application for reinstatement is made less than 3 years after the date of the motor accident, the claim
-- is to be reinstated if the court or Commission is satisfied that the claimant has a full and satisfactory explanation
-- for the failure". s 85B(7): if made 3 years or more after the accident, also "(b) the total damages of all kinds likely
-- to be awarded ... are not less than 25% of the maximum amount that may be awarded for non-economic loss under section
-- 134 as at the date of the motor accident". The s 134 maximum at that date (indexed under s 146) is asked. "is to be
-- reinstated if": JUST FALSE where the conditions fail.
@export If my claim was taken to be withdrawn for want of particulars, must it be reinstated on my application (s 85B(4), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the day I apply for reinstatement` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply for reinstatement (to the Personal Injury Commission, or to a court if the claim is exempt from assessment)
      `I have a full and satisfactory explanation for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission or court is satisfied you have a full and satisfactory explanation for not providing the particulars (a full account of your conduct since the accident, such that a reasonable person in your position would have done the same)
      `the total damages I am likely to be awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The total damages of all kinds, in dollars, likely to be awarded to you if the claim succeeds
      `the non-economic loss maximum at the date of the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum that could be awarded for non-economic loss under section 134 as at the date of the accident, in dollars ($284,000 in the Act, indexed each year under section 146)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my withdrawn claim be reinstated` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I have a full and satisfactory explanation for the failure`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 85B(6), (7)(a)
           IF `the day I apply for reinstatement` `is before` (`the day of the accident` `plus years` 3) THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 85B(6)
           IF `the damages are large enough` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 85B(7)(b)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the damages are large enough` MEANS `the total damages I am likely to be awarded` AT LEAST ((`the non-economic loss maximum at the date of the accident` TIMES 25) DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `ss 108, 109, 85(4), 86(4) -- going to court`

-- s 109(1) "A claimant is not entitled to commence proceedings in respect of a claim more than 3 years after-- (a) the date
-- of the motor accident ..., or (b) if the claim is made in respect of the death of a person--the date of death, except
-- with the leave of the court". s 109(2) "Time does not run ... from the time that a claim has been referred to the
-- Commission for assessment and until 2 months after a certificate as to the assessment or exemption from assessment is
-- issued." The paused days are added to the 3 years, but only where the referral was made while time was still running
-- (fork F8). Where the claim has been referred and no certificate has yet issued, time is stopped and there is no last
-- day yet (NOTHING). s 109(5): the Limitation Act 1969 does not apply.
GIVEN `the relevant day` IS A DATE
      `the claim was referred for assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was referred` IS A DATE
      `the day the certificate was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day without leave` `the relevant day` `the claim was referred for assessment` `the day it was referred` `the day the certificate was issued` MEANS
    IF `the pause counts`
    THEN `the three years end` `plus days` (`the days from` `the day it was referred` `to` (`the day the certificate was issued` `plus months` 2))
    ELSE `the three years end`
    WHERE
        `the three years end` MEANS `the relevant day` `plus years` 3
        `the pause counts` MEANS `the claim was referred for assessment` AND (NOT (`the day it was referred` `is after` `the three years end`))

@export What is the last day I may commence court proceedings on my claim without the court's leave (s 109(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the claim is for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for the death of a person
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died (any day if the claim is not for a death)
      `the claim was referred for assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim has been referred to the Personal Injury Commission (or earlier the claims assessment service) for assessment or a certificate of exemption
      `the day it was referred` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was referred (any day if not)
      `a certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a certificate of assessment or of exemption from assessment has been issued on the referral
      `the day the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc The day the certificate was issued (any day if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`What is the last day to commence proceedings without leave` MEANS
    IF `the claim was referred for assessment` AND (NOT `a certificate has been issued`) AND (NOT (`the day it was referred` `is after` (`the relevant day` `plus years` 3)))
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (time is not running: no last day yet, s 109(2))
    ELSE JUST (`the last day without leave` `the relevant day` `the claim was referred for assessment` `the day it was referred` `the day the certificate was issued`)
    WHERE
        `the relevant day` MEANS `the relevant date` `the day of the accident` `the claim is for a death` `the day of death`

-- s 108(1) "a claimant is not entitled to commence court proceedings ... unless-- (a) a certificate has been issued ...
-- under section 92 (Claims exempt from assessment), or (b) a certificate has been issued ... under section 94 (Assessment
-- of claims)" (subject to the Personal Injury Commission Act 2020 Division 3.2, not deposited). s 85(4): while the
-- claimant fails without reasonable excuse to co-operate, "court proceedings cannot be commenced". s 86(4)(b): the same
-- while the claimant fails without reasonable excuse to undergo a requested examination or assessment. s 109(3) "The
-- leave of the court must not be granted unless-- (a) the claimant provides a full and satisfactory explanation to the
-- court for the delay, and (b) the total damages ... likely to be awarded ... are not less than 25% of the maximum amount
-- that may be awarded for non-economic loss under section 134 as at the date of the relevant motor accident." s 109(4):
-- (b) does not apply to a claimant legally incapacitated by age or mental capacity. Whether leave is granted beyond that
-- is the court's (asked).
@export Am I entitled to commence court proceedings on my claim on the day I plan to (ss 85(4), 86(4), 108, 109)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the claim is for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for the death of a person
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died (any day if the claim is not for a death)
      `a certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Personal Injury Commission has issued a certificate of assessment (s 94) or of exemption from assessment (s 92) for the claim
      `the claim was referred for assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim was referred to the Commission for assessment or a certificate of exemption
      `the day it was referred` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was referred (any day if not)
      `the day the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc The day the certificate was issued (any day if none)
      `the day I plan to commence` IS A DATE @desc The day you plan to commence the court proceedings
      `I am failing without reasonable excuse to co-operate or be examined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are currently failing, without reasonable excuse, to co-operate with the insurer as section 85 requires, or to undergo a medical examination or assessment validly requested under section 86
      `I can give the court a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can give the court a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay in commencing proceedings (matters only if you are late)
      `the total damages I am likely to be awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The total damages of all kinds, in dollars, likely to be awarded to you if the claim succeeds (matters only if you are late)
      `the non-economic loss maximum at the date of the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum that could be awarded for non-economic loss under section 134 as at the date of the accident, in dollars ($284,000 in the Act, indexed each year under section 146)
      `I am legally incapacitated by age or mental capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are legally incapacitated because of your age (a minor) or your mental capacity
      `the court grants leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court grants leave to commence late (matters only if you are late and the conditions for leave are met)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to commence court proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `a certificate has been issued`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 108(1)
           IF `I am failing without reasonable excuse to co-operate or be examined` THEN JUST FALSE  -- ss 85(4), 86(4)(b)
           IF (NOT (`the day I plan to commence` `is after` `the last day`)) THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 109(1)
           IF (NOT `I can give the court a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 109(3)(a)
           IF (NOT (`I am legally incapacitated by age or mental capacity` OR `the damages are large enough`)) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 109(3)(b), (4)
           IF `the court grants leave` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 109(1) "except with the leave of the court"
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day without leave` (`the relevant date` `the day of the accident` `the claim is for a death` `the day of death`) `the claim was referred for assessment` `the day it was referred` `the day the certificate was issued`
        `the damages are large enough` MEANS `the total damages I am likely to be awarded` AT LEAST ((`the non-economic loss maximum at the date of the accident` TIMES 25) DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `s 110 -- the insurer's notice to commence proceedings`

-- s 110(1) the insurer "may give the claimant notice requiring the claimant to commence court proceedings ... if-- (a)
-- the claimant has been entitled to commence the proceedings for a period of at least 6 months, and (b) at least 18
-- months have elapsed since the date of the motor accident". s 110(2) "The claimant must comply with the notice within 3
-- months after its receipt." s 110(3) "If the claimant does not comply ..., the claimant is taken to have withdrawn the
-- claim." s 110(4), (5): the court may reinstate it on a full and satisfactory explanation (asked). The conditions of
-- s 110(1) are tested on the day the claimant received the notice (fork F9).
GIVEN `the days in the three months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 110(2) -- the claimant must commence court proceedings within 3 months after receiving the notice` `the days in the three months` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `commence court proceedings`
    WITHIN `the days in the three months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "court proceedings not commenced within 3 months after receiving the insurer's notice (s 110(2)); the claimant is taken to have withdrawn the claim (s 110(3))"

@export The insurer has given me notice to commence court proceedings: is my claim taken to have been withdrawn (s 110)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the day I became entitled to commence proceedings` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became entitled to commence court proceedings on the claim (for example the day a certificate of assessment or exemption was issued)
      `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the insurer's notice requiring you to commence court proceedings
      `I have commenced proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have commenced court proceedings on the claim
      `the day I commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced them (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `the court has reinstated my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has reinstated the claim on your application (s 110(4), (5))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my claim withdrawn for not commencing proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`the day I became entitled to commence proceedings` `plus months` 6) `is after` `the day I received the notice` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 110(1)(a)
           IF (`the day of the accident` `plus months` 18) `is after` `the day I received the notice` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 110(1)(b)
           IF `complied in time` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT (`I have commenced proceedings` OR `the time is up`)) THEN JUST FALSE  -- the 3 months have not yet run
           IF `the court has reinstated my claim` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 110(5)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- s 110(3)
    WHERE
        `the window` MEANS `the days in the` 3 `months after` `the day I received the notice`
        `complied in time` MEANS
            `the rule was kept` (`s 110(2) -- the claimant must commence court proceedings within 3 months after receiving the notice` `the window`) `the claimant` `commence court proceedings` `I have commenced proceedings` (`the days from` `the day I received the notice` `to` `the day I commenced`) (`the days from` `the day I received the notice` `to` `today`)
        `the time is up` MEANS `the days from` `the day I received the notice` `to` `today` GREATER THAN `the window`
